# Anthropic Prompts Library

A central library of Anthropic/Claude system prompts, skills, and reference material lives at:

```
/Users/abhishek/Prompts/Anthropic/
```

## What's available

### Skills (auto-discovered in Claude Code & TRAE)
- `code-review` — multi-level code review (low → max)
- `dataviz` — data visualization design guidance
- `deep-research` — fan-out web research with cited reports
- `run-skill-generator` — generate per-project run skills

### System prompts (browse for reference)
- **Root `*.md`** — current model prompts: `claude-opus-4.8.md`, `claude-sonnet-5.md`, `claude-design.md`, `visualize.md`, `research_instructions.md`, `anthropic_reminders.md`, etc.
- **`Official/`** — dated release-notes archive (2024-07-12 → 2026-05-28)
- **`old/`** — legacy prompts (Claude 3.7, 4.1, 4.5)
- **`raw/`** — unedited raw system prompts (opus/sonnet 4.6, ±tools)

### Claude Code tool docs & slash commands
`Claude Code/bundled-skills/` contains `glob-tool.md`, `grep-tool.md`, `init.md`, `compact.md`, `debug.md`, `verify.md`, `run.md`, `loop.md`, `schedule.md`, `batch.md`, `simplify.md`, `security-review.md`, and more.

## How to use

```bash
# Browse the library
ls /Users/abhishek/Prompts/Anthropic/

# Read the master index
cat /Users/abhishek/Prompts/Anthropic/README.md

# Agent discovery guide
cat /Users/abhishek/Prompts/Anthropic/AGENTS.md

# Search across all prompts
grep -ri "<keyword>" /Users/abhishek/Prompts/Anthropic/
```

## When to reference this library

- **Building a custom agent** → check existing system prompts for patterns
- **Needing Claude's exact behavior** → read the model-specific prompt
- **Code review** → invoke the `code-review` skill or read the level templates
- **Research tasks** → invoke `deep-research` skill or read `research_instructions.md`
- **Design/artifact work** → read `claude-design.md` or `visualize.md`
- **Safety/reminders** → read `anthropic_reminders.md`

Single source of truth — edit in place, all tools see updates via symlinks.
